# The parameter is `any`, and an Item is what was seen. That is a prediction: it is tested, and both ways to fail it leave by an unlikely edge to one block that reads the property by name. The way that holds falls through to a plain load.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="weigh" role=Source
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:ObjectFields
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[notCell]] = BitAnd(b@[[item]], {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[notCell]], Terminal
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:Unlikely:#[[byName]], Else:#[[cell]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[cell]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors: #0
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[shape]] = Load(b@[[item]], offset = 12, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:AOTObject_shapeWord
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:ObjectFields
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isItem]] = Equal(b@[[shape]], $
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isItem]], Terminal
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#[[read]], Else:Unlikely:#[[byName]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[read]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors: #[[cell]]
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[weight]] = Load(b@[[item]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK: BB#[[byName]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors: #0, #[[cell]]
# CHECK-NEXT: Patchpoint(b@[[item]]:{{*}}ExitsSideways
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The frame is set up only in the block that calls: the way that holds runs without one.
